# derived: vk_check.py says so in its output while this line stands; a capture has no such line.
# GM-1d: what deqp-vk's subset must answer on the real 780M. Not a capture yet: no Linux run of the subset on the chip
# exists (the host's GPU drives the desk's display and gets no jobs, the Mini-PC's CachyOS live run predates this).
# Made so: every case a device with the capture's features can run must Pass; RADV of this same Mesa says on the fake
# 780M (vulkaninfo equal to the chip's, host/tests/gm/40-vk-proof.sh checks it each run) that it supports every case.
# A capture on CachyOS replaces this file: vkdiff.py deqp-ref <deqp-vk's stdout>.
